     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day, with single doses of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg PO per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- Another dose, if 1700 mg was a typo.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
